{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DECISION RECORDED (operator, settled — not re-litigated during implementation): the project default flips to Bedrock. `rebar.toml` now carries a top-level `[llm]` table with both a scalar `model` and an `[llm.model_classes]` table, all three ids taken verbatim from `.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml`.\n\nAlternative rejected: keep Anthropic as the default and make the opt-in loud (make target / doctor warning). Cheaper on onboarding, but it advertises the dogfooding gap instead of closing it.\n\nCost accepted knowingly: local LLM gates now need working AWS credentials on the ambient chain plus a resolvable region. Mitigation is the documented one-line OPT-OUT, `REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE=\\\"\\$PWD/.github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml\\\"`, exercised by a test rather than only written down.\n\nDeparture from this ticket's own Testing note, on operator instruction: the plan said 'Do NOT set [llm] model as a scalar'. Both are set. The scalar is NOT used as a substitute for the class table (which would collapse the per-pass frontier/standard split — the eb58 trap) but as a COMPANION: cfg.model is a second resolution path the class table cannot reach, defaulting to the bare literal claude-opus-4-8 which infers provider anthropic. Setting only the classes would have left the f124 ambient-default provider leak open in local dev. MEASURED here: with the class table alone, LLMConfig.from_env().model resolved to 'claude-opus-4-8'; with both, to 'bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8'.\n\nMEASURED AFTER (clean env, no REBAR_LLM_*, repo_root pinned at the checkout):\n  frontier -> bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n  standard -> bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n  trivial  -> bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\n  cfg.model -> bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n(Before, same conditions: anthropic:claude-opus-4-8 / anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6 / anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5, and cfg.model claude-opus-4-8.)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785807472214442001,"uuid":"a18b4f5a-348a-4e2a-a716-67b731305c02"}